/-!
# Lane C3 (snapshot copied into Lane C, namespace CKLaneC.S3) — Lagrange–Taylor remainders for derivative chains on `[0,1]`

For a chain `f₀, …, fₙ` with `fᵢ' = fᵢ₊₁` on `[0,1]` there is `θ ∈ (0,1)` with
`f₀ 1 = Σ_{i<n} fᵢ 0 / i! + fₙ θ / n!` (orders `n = 1, …, 5`), by iterated Rolle.
(Generated by tools/gen_taylor_chain.py; proof pattern from
`GeneralCK.Certificates.E8CompactAnchorTaylor3.exists_remainder`.)
-/

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option relaxedAutoImplicit false
set_option linter.unusedSimpArgs false

